m sea level to 5130 meters above sea level (Pratali et al. [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B74">64</xref>]).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="PM2011-275857.002"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Chest ultrasonography revealed an increased number of ULCs within 10 minutes after immersion in 45% of 14 top-level breath-hold deep divers, which resolved completely after 24 hours (Frassi et al. [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B75">71</xref>]).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="PM2011-275857.003"/></fig></floats-group></article>